    "Severe Class Imbalance: Positive reviews dominate at 81.24% raw (166,581 rows) and 75.2% clean (83,084 rows). Neutral reviews represent only 4.99% raw and 5.82% clean, requiring class-weighted loss and macro-averaged metrics.",
    "Critical Duplicate Leakage Risk: Found 34,375 completely identical rows and 94,294 duplicates on (Review, Summary). Removing review text duplicates reduces the dataset from 205,052 to 110,486 unique reviews, preventing severe train/test data leakage.",
    "Data Corruption Handled: Detected and removed 3 corrupted row(s) where product names shifted into the 'Rate' column.",
    "Missing Review Titles vs. Detailed Summaries: 24,664 rows (12.0%) lacked a short 'Review' title, whereas only 11 rows lacked a 'Summary'. Using 'Summary' as primary review text guarantees informative review semantics.",
    "Review Length by Sentiment: Dissatisfied customers express negative feedback with significantly longer text (average 14.8 words) compared to positive reviews (average 13.8 words), which often consist of terse praise (e.g., 'awesome', 'good product').",
    "Label-Rating Discrepancies: While 5-star ratings are 96.6% positive, 740 reviews with 5 stars actually carry negative sentiment text, and 1032 reviews with 1 star express positive sentiment, proving star ratings alone are insufficient as text sentiment proxies."
